    {
      "id": "8d8ac2f8d0e3fb746472a842bfed2b4e29c3eded",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1492885628,
          "type": null,
          "body": "No, the existing code is correct. It is a bitfield; the correct thing to do to test if both values are set is to bitwise OR the selected bits to create a mask, as currently done, and then test \n\n[`(ssl_session->state & SSL_EXTENDED_MASTER_SECRET_MASK) == SSL_EXTENDED_MASTER_SECRET_MASK)`](epan/dissectors/packet-tls-utils.c#L4282)\n\nA bitwise AND of `SSL_CLIENT_EXTENDED_MASTER_SECRET (1<<7)` and `SSL_SERVER_EXTENDED_MASTER_SECRET (1<<8)` produces 0.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-07-30T01:31:47.972Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-07-30T01:31:47.972Z",
